{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgBHd9mMMVPvHnGELrjdJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All six acceptance criteria pass on the current tree. I made no code changes this iteration: the code and seed data from the previous pass already satisfy them.\n\nThe one failure last time was the live check `GET /api/links` looking for `\"slug\":\"zurdo\"`. The server's body does contain that string (`[{\"slug\":\"carol\",...},{\"slug\":\"zurdo\",...}]`), and it matches on re-check. The earlier failure was most likely a transient or stale response from the dev server; I can't confirm that from here. I did not restart or touch the server on port 8787.\n\nChecks run from the worktree:\n- **serve with unreadable data:** `serve --data testdata` exits 1 and prints `shortlink serve: read testdata: read testdata: is a directory`, which names the path. The doubled `read testdata:` comes from the store's existing error wrapping.\n- **Live server:** `/healthz` returns 200 `ok`. `/api/links` includes the zurdo link. `/api/links/carol` returns the carol URL. `/api/links/nope` returns 404. `/zurdo` returns `302 https://github.com/ElOrlis/zurdo` without following it.\n- **Tree hygiene:** `gofmt -l .` is empty, `go vet ./...` and `go vet -tags=preauthored ./...` are clean, and `go test -tags=preauthored -count=1 ./...` passes. The untagged `go test -count=1 ./...` also passes, as CLAUDE.md requires.\n\nThe working tree is unchanged from the previous iteration's uncommitted edits (`cmd/shortlink/main.go`, its test, `internal/store/store.go`, `internal/server/server.go`, and `testdata/seed.json`)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":748,"cache_read_input_tokens":35234,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":748},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed